[thin] The separate tube bores and flat signal slot follow the mounting row. The straight drain-to-slot web is 1.0625 mm and the closest round-bore web is 1.3148 mm; their entrance chamfers reduce those figures locally to 0.4625 and 0.5148 mm. The narrow entrance regions are short tapers into the full 10 mm puck, rather than freestanding retaining walls. The four round bores retain the selected diameters, 0.4 mm entrance chamfers and 9.2 mm contact length. This geometry supplies spacing and hand adjustment; the unprinted layout has no load-capacity or endurance acceptance.
alternatives: Greater flavor spread or a farther-forward drain thickens the webs but increases the displacement from the mounting slots; a round cable hole needs a larger rear offset to retain a separate drain wall. Smaller entrance chamfers increase local stock but shorten the tube lead-in or ribbon threading relief. A joined opening removes the web but does not preserve four separate round tube passages.
