[thin] The outer stock around the three beverage bores is at least 1.9371 mm through the straight contact region. The 0.6 mm rim ease and 0.4 mm tube entrances reduce it at the upper and lower edges. Those tapers ease feeding the bare tube ends and expanding the braid over the puck. The round stock is centered on the beverage-bore circumcentre, so all three receive the same nominal exterior backing. The nominal braided envelope is 34 mm inside the 34.93 mm installation hole; physical braid passage and the unprinted layout remain unmeasured.
alternatives: Increasing the puck diameter adds backing but consumes the 0.465 mm nominal radial braid clearance. Moving the bores inward changes the relationship to the mounting slots and tube-to-tube webs. Reducing the rim or tube-entry chamfers adds stock at the edges but reduces their feeding relief; it does not increase the straight-bore backing.
